    "html": "<p>Hi {{first_name}},</p>\n<p>Nobody hands a four-year-old a contract. But most of us signed one anyway.</p>\n<p>It goes something like this: <em>Be agreeable and you\u2019ll be safe. Other people\u2019s feelings are your job. Your needs are a burden. Conflict means something went wrong. If you\u2019re good enough, you\u2019ll be treated fairly.</em></p>\n<p>I call it the Good Person Contract. It made sense when you were small. Keeping the adults happy was how you stayed safe.</p>\n<p>The trouble is that most people are still living by it at forty, fifty, sixty, and wondering why they\u2019re tired.</p>\n<p>Read those terms as if a stranger offered them to you as a job. No pay, no end date, no right to renegotiate. You\u2019d turn it down in a second.</p>\n<p>Chapter 2 of <em>Shadow Persuasion</em> goes through the contract clause by clause, with the adult version of each one.</p>\n<p><a href=\"%7B%7Bbook_link%7D%7D\">See what\u2019s in the book</a></p>\n<p>Nate</p>",
